{"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "dc7d3a1d-5783-41f6-8178-9c20fa5f8577", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "I have created the Python/C polyglot in [main.py.c](file:///tmp/xhs-c6-host-9_r1tj_v/polyglot/main.py.c) (mounted at `/app/polyglot/main.py.c` inside the container).\n\n### How it works\n- **In C**: `#/* ... #*/` forms a multi-line comment (`/* ... */`) after `#`, which preprocesses to an empty null directive (`#`), hiding the Python section. The trailing `//\"\"\"` is treated as a single-line C comment.\n- **In Python**: `#/*` is a comment, followed by the Python implementation and `r\"\"\"`, which opens a raw triple-quoted string literal that spans the entire C implementation until closed by `//\"\"\"` at the end of the file.\n- Both implementations compute and print the $N$-th Fibonacci number ($f(0) = 0, f(1) = 1, \\dots$) with arbitrary precision.\n", "duration_seconds": 81.323061171, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 22214, "output_tokens": 5348, "thinking_tokens": 3844, "cache_read_tokens": 54837, "total_tokens": 27562}}}